0
00:00:04,037 --> 00:00:06,006
Tyra: LOTS OF GIRLS
GROW UP WANTING TO BE MODELS

1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,074
BECAUSE THEY THINK
IT'S GLAMOROUS, EXCITING,

2
00:00:08,074 --> 00:00:10,444
AND, YOU KNOW, FUN.

3
00:00:10,444 --> 00:00:12,212
WRONG!

4
00:00:12,212 --> 00:00:13,981
- Catie: (cries)
- Jenascia: THOSE BITCHES!

5
00:00:13,981 --> 00:00:16,049
Tyra: "AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL" HAS TAKEN

6
00:00:16,049 --> 00:00:18,352
THIS GROUP OF GIRLS
ON QUITE A JOURNEY.

7
00:00:18,352 --> 00:00:20,454
THEY'VE POSED NUDE,
THEY'VE GOTTEN

8
00:00:20,454 --> 00:00:23,357
DRASTIC MAKEOVERS
AND THEY'VE DONE SOME REALLY

9
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:25,459
DIFFICULT PHOTO SHOOTS
THAT HAVE PUSHED THEM

10
00:00:25,459 --> 00:00:27,661
TO THEIR LIMITS.

11
00:00:27,661 --> 00:00:31,565
FIND OUT HOW THIS GROUP OF 12
GOT DOWN TO THE FINAL FOUR.

12
00:00:31,565 --> 00:00:35,569
IT ALL BEGINS NOW WITH MOMENTS
YOU'VE NEVER SEEN BEFORE,

13
00:00:35,569 --> 00:00:36,970
INCLUDING THE WILDEST PRANK...

14
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:38,105
(laughter)

15
00:00:38,105 --> 00:00:40,007
Tyra: THE MOST
EMBARRASSING MOMENTS...

16
00:00:40,007 --> 00:00:41,542
Janice: WHAT THE HELL
WAS THAT?

17
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:43,110
Tyra: AND WHAT HAPPENS
WHEN THE JUDGES TURN

18
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:44,211
ON EACH OTHER.

19
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:46,380
Jay: WE'RE TALKING
SILICONE VALLEY

20
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:48,115
AT THE OTHER END OF THE TABLE.

21
00:00:48,115 --> 00:00:50,117
Janice: OH, STAND UP.
LET'S SEE THE GIRDLE
YOU'RE WEARING.

22
00:00:50,117 --> 00:00:52,019
Jay: JANICE, YOURS IS ALREADY
SURGICALLY CINCHED.

23
00:00:52,019 --> 00:00:54,121
I SNAP ONE THREAD,
AND IT'S DOWN.

24
00:00:54,121 --> 00:00:56,757
♪♪♪

25
00:01:27,154 --> 00:01:29,423
Tyra: FOR THE SECOND SEASON
OF "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,"

26
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:32,192
WE HAD THOUSANDS AND THOUSANDS
OF APPLICANTS.

27
00:01:32,192 --> 00:01:34,695
THIS TIME WE CHOSE 12.

28
00:01:36,463 --> 00:01:39,099
Shandi: AND THE REASON
I WANT TO BE THE NEXT TOP MODEL

29
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:41,602
IS BECAUSE I AM TIRED OF WORKING
AT WALGREENS.

30
00:01:41,602 --> 00:01:44,137
Mercedes: MY FLAVOR
WOULD BE THAT I'M SASSY.

31
00:01:44,137 --> 00:01:47,107
Heather: I JUST TURNED 18
THREE DAYS AGO.

32
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:49,610
Jenascia: WHEN I SHOWER,
I LIKE TO PLAY SOME HOOPS.

33
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:51,178
THE BALL'S OVER HERE SOMEWHERE.

34
00:01:51,178 --> 00:01:52,312
Anna: SAY, "WE'RE GOING
TO THE OTHER ROOM."

35
00:01:52,312 --> 00:01:53,280
Makarious: (babbling)
WE GO OTHER ROOM.

36
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:54,581
Anna: OKAY.

37
00:01:54,581 --> 00:01:56,149
Xiomara: PLEASE, CALL ME XIOMI.
DON'T CALL ME XIOMARA.

38
00:01:56,149 --> 00:01:57,417
IT'S JUST TOO HARD,
UNLESS YOU CAN REALLY SAY IT

39
00:01:57,417 --> 00:01:59,519
AND ROLL YOUR R's--
(rolling R's) XIOMARA.

40
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:00,687
Bethany: I WAS BORN HERE
IN HOUSTON.

41
00:02:00,687 --> 00:02:03,223
YEE-HA! WHA-WHA-WHA!

42
00:02:03,223 --> 00:02:05,158
Yoanna: WE DON'T REALLY HAVE
A GREAT DEPARTMENT STORE

43
00:02:05,158 --> 00:02:07,194
HERE IN JACKSONVILLE,
WHICH IS REALLY DEPRESSING.

44
00:02:07,194 --> 00:02:10,597
Catie: I KNOW WHAT MAKES ME
DIFFERENT IS I HATE MODELS.

45
00:02:10,597 --> 00:02:12,766
Camille: THERE COMES A TIME
WHEN PEOPLE GET ON YOUR NERVES,

46
00:02:12,766 --> 00:02:15,202
AND THEY BOTHER YOU,
AND THEY KIND OF ANNOY YOU.

47
00:02:15,202 --> 00:02:16,403
April: I'M A FIGHTER
TO THE DEATH.

48
00:02:16,403 --> 00:02:18,238
LET THE GAMES BEGIN.

49
00:02:18,238 --> 00:02:19,740
Sara: I HAVE WHAT IT TAKES,
OF COURSE.

50
00:02:22,509 --> 00:02:25,545
Anna: COULD YOU TELL ME
WHERE BROAD STREET IS?

51
00:02:25,545 --> 00:02:27,014
Tyra: AFTER BRINGING
THE GIRLS FROM ALL OVER

52
00:02:27,014 --> 00:02:29,616
THE COUNTRY TO NEW YORK CITY,
I'VE DECIDED TO DO SOMETHING

53
00:02:29,616 --> 00:02:31,218
TOTALLY DIFFERENT THIS YEAR.

54
00:02:31,218 --> 00:02:33,687
I JUST WANTED TO SHAKE IT UP
AND SHOCK THE GIRLS.

55
00:02:33,687 --> 00:02:35,689
I'M NOT WASTING ANY TIME.

56
00:02:35,689 --> 00:02:38,225
I'M THROWING YOU
STRAIGHT ON A RUNWAY.

57
00:02:38,225 --> 00:02:40,027
YOU'RE GONNA BE DOING IT
IN FRONT OF THE BEST

58
00:02:40,027 --> 00:02:41,561
OF NEW YORK--
OUR FIREFIGHTERS

59
00:02:41,561 --> 00:02:42,996
AND OUR MILITARY.

60
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:44,564
Jenascia: ARE YOU KIDDING ME?

61
00:02:44,564 --> 00:02:47,200
J.: OKAY, GIRLS,
YOU HAVE EXACTLY 30 MINUTES

62
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,235
TO GET READY.

63
00:02:48,235 --> 00:02:50,370
YOU EACH WILL BE WEARING
THREE OUTFITS.

64
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:53,407
IT'S CRITICAL
THAT YOU REMEMBER YOUR ORDER.

65
00:02:53,407 --> 00:02:57,411
REMEMBER, FOLLOW THE HAIR
AND MAKEUP INSTRUCTIONS.

66
00:02:57,411 --> 00:02:58,578
Anna: I FEEL LIKE
THE ROADRUNNER RIGHT NOW.

67
00:02:58,578 --> 00:02:59,713
I'M TRYING TO BE VERY FAST.

68
00:02:59,713 --> 00:03:02,015
Sara: I'M EXCITED.

69
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:03,183
Catie: I USUALLY
LIKE SURPRISES,

70
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:05,652
BUT THIS IS
TO A DIFFERENT MAGNITUDE.

71
00:03:05,652 --> 00:03:07,621
J.: PRESSURE IS ON!

72
00:03:07,621 --> 00:03:11,058
Tyra: APRIL GOT CAUGHT UP
IN THE CHAOS AND LOST CONTROL.

73
00:03:11,058 --> 00:03:12,259
April: I HAVE
THE WRONG OUTFIT ON.

74
00:03:12,259 --> 00:03:13,694
Jenascia: ALL OF A SUDDEN
I SAW THAT APRIL--

75
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:15,662
SHE HAD HER SECOND OUTFIT
ON FIRST.

76
00:03:15,662 --> 00:03:17,364
April: AND I START
TO CRY IMMEDIATELY,

77
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:20,267
BECAUSE I AM SO STRESSED
THAT I MANAGED TO SCREW UP

78
00:03:20,267 --> 00:03:22,469
WITHIN THE FIRST TEN MINUTES
OF THIS COMPETITION.

79
00:03:22,469 --> 00:03:24,371
Jenascia: HERE, I'LL DO THAT.
YOU DO THIS.

80
00:03:24,371 --> 00:03:25,639
April: THE ONLY THING
THAT IS LITERALLY KEEPING

81
00:03:25,639 --> 00:03:28,241
MY KNEES FROM COLLAPSING
ON ME RIGHT NOW IS THE FACT

82
00:03:28,241 --> 00:03:29,543
THAT JENASCIA IS AT MY SIDE.

83
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:30,610
I'M THINKING, "I OWE HER."

84
00:03:33,346 --> 00:03:34,614
Jenascia: I'M NOT REALLY
THAT NICE OF A PERSON.

85
00:03:34,614 --> 00:03:36,416
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT'S COME OVER ME.

86
00:03:36,416 --> 00:03:39,553
♪♪♪

87
00:03:39,553 --> 00:03:41,488
Tyra: THAT RUNWAY SHOW

88
00:03:41,488 --> 00:03:44,524
EXPOSED THEM AS AMATEURS,
AND IT SHOWED JUST HOW FAR

89
00:03:44,524 --> 00:03:46,626
THEY HAD TO GO.

90
00:03:46,626 --> 00:03:48,628
J.: OKAY, GIRLS,
PERSONALLY, I THINK

91
00:03:48,628 --> 00:03:51,465
YOU ALL SUCKED, ACTUALLY.

92
00:03:51,465 --> 00:03:54,034
Tyra: THE NEXT MORNING,
THE GIRLS WOKE UP SUPER EARLY

93
00:03:54,034 --> 00:03:57,537
FOR THEIR FIRST PHOTO SHOOT,
BUT JENASCIA WAS SOUND ASLEEP,

94
00:03:57,537 --> 00:04:01,208
AND APRIL WAS TORN
ABOUT WHAT TO DO.

95
00:04:01,208 --> 00:04:02,476
April: IF I RUN UPSTAIRS,
ARE YOU GUYS GONNA MAKE SURE

96
00:04:02,476 --> 00:04:03,577
THEY DON'T LEAVE WITHOUT ME
OR NO?

97
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:05,045
PROBABLY NOT, RIGHT?

98
00:04:05,045 --> 00:04:06,513
Anna: RUN UP INSIDE AND SEE.

99
00:04:06,513 --> 00:04:08,181
April: I AM NOT ABLE
TO HELP HER OUT

100
00:04:08,181 --> 00:04:10,584
AND GET HER IN THAT VAN
WITHOUT JEOPARDIZING

101
00:04:10,584 --> 00:04:13,520
EVERY SINGLE OTHER PERSON'S
ABILITY TO GET TO THE SHOOT.

102
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:16,423
SHE HELPED ME OUT ON THE RUNWAY,
AND THAT'S TEARING ME UP INSIDE.

103
00:04:19,526 --> 00:04:21,128
Tyra: THE MODELS HAD NO IDEA
WHAT TYPE OF SHOOT

104
00:04:21,128 --> 00:04:22,529
THEY WERE IN FOR.

105
00:04:22,529 --> 00:04:25,065
Ed: THIS IS THE MAJOR PART
OF YOUR COSTUME RIGHT HERE.

106
00:04:25,065 --> 00:04:27,601
YOUR BODY'S GONNA BE COVERED
IN JEWELS AND BODY PAINT.

107
00:04:27,601 --> 00:04:30,437
Anna: SO OUR WHOLE BODY'S
COVERED IN THE PAINT?

108
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:32,405
Ed: YEAH, YOUR BODIES
WILL BE COVERED IN PAINT, YES.

109
00:04:32,405 --> 00:04:35,142
Nigel: YES, BUT, I MEAN,
OBVIOUSLY YOU ARE GONNA BE NUDE.

110
00:04:35,142 --> 00:04:37,511
Tyra: ANNA, A WIFE
AND MOTHER, WAS SHOCKED.

111
00:04:37,511 --> 00:04:39,012
Nigel: I SEE WE ONLY HAVE 11.

112
00:04:39,012 --> 00:04:42,082
Tyra: AND JENASCIA
WAS STILL ASLEEP.

113
00:04:42,082 --> 00:04:43,383
Nigel: WELL, WE'LL HAVE
TO GET A WAKE-UP CALL INTO HER.

114
00:04:43,383 --> 00:04:46,386
(telephone rings)

115
00:04:46,386 --> 00:04:48,655
(sighs)

116
00:04:48,655 --> 00:04:50,490
- Jenascia: HELLO?
- Jim: IS THIS JENASCIA?

117
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:52,659
Jenascia: I DON'T KNOW
HOW THIS HAPPENED!

118
00:04:52,659 --> 00:04:55,061
Jim: SO GET YOURSELF TOGETHER
AND GET HERE ASAP.

119
00:04:55,061 --> 00:04:58,231
Jenascia: THOSE
(bleep) BITCHES!

120
00:04:58,231 --> 00:05:01,201
THEY LET ME JUST SLEEP.
I DON'T KNOW.

121
00:05:01,201 --> 00:05:04,070
THEY MUST HAVE TIPPED AROUND
LIKE... MICE THIS MORNING,

122
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:06,072
'CAUSE I DIDN'T HEAR
A DAMN THING.

123
00:05:06,072 --> 00:05:09,142
I WAS SO NAIVE TO THINK THAT
THE OTHER GIRLS WERE ACTUALLY

124
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:11,478
GONNA HELP ME OUT,
EVEN THOUGH I HAD HELPED

125
00:05:11,478 --> 00:05:13,413
SOME OF THEM OUT.

126
00:05:13,413 --> 00:05:15,248
- Camille: FOCUS ON...
- Jenascia: ME.

127
00:05:15,248 --> 00:05:16,750
Camille: YEAH,
WHAT YOU NEED TO DO RIGHT NOW

128
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:19,352
IS GET THE BEST PICTURES.

129
00:05:19,352 --> 00:05:21,321
Jenascia: I JUST DIDN'T KNOW
THAT SOME PEOPLE WERE

130
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:23,256
THAT THREATENED BY ME.

131
00:05:23,256 --> 00:05:24,391
BITCHES!

132
00:05:27,527 --> 00:05:29,362
Catie: MY DAD--
I DON'T THINK HE WAS COMFORTABLE

133
00:05:29,362 --> 00:05:30,764
WITH ME DOING NUDE.

134
00:05:30,764 --> 00:05:33,633
YOU KNOW, IF I'M DOING NUDE,
AT LEAST I'M BEING AN ANGEL.

135
00:05:33,633 --> 00:05:35,502
Sara: GRANDMA, DON'T HATE ME!

136
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:37,504
♪♪♪

137
00:05:44,644 --> 00:05:47,080
Tyra: WHILE JENASCIA WAS
PREPPING FOR HER PHOTO SHOOT,

138
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:50,050
ANNA WAS HAVING A MORAL CRISIS.

139
00:05:50,050 --> 00:05:51,718
Anna: I SAT THERE IN THE ROOM,
AND I SAW THESE GIRLS.

140
00:05:51,718 --> 00:05:54,487
THEIR BREASTS WERE HANGING OUT
AND NIPPLES SHOWING.

141
00:05:54,487 --> 00:05:57,557
I CAN'T JUST IMAGINE
SOMEONE ELSE HERE AND DOWN THERE

142
00:05:57,557 --> 00:05:59,659
EXCEPT MY HUSBAND, YOU KNOW?

143
00:05:59,659 --> 00:06:02,095
AND IF I SHOW IT
TO THE WHOLE WORLD, YOU KNOW,

144
00:06:02,095 --> 00:06:04,731
WHAT'S SO SPECIAL WHEN I...

145
00:06:04,731 --> 00:06:06,066
(crying)
I JUST CAN'T.

146
00:06:06,066 --> 00:06:06,766
I CANNOT DO IT.

147
00:06:08,068 --> 00:06:10,170
Tyra: WHEN IT CAME
TO THE FIRST ELIMINATION,

148
00:06:10,170 --> 00:06:13,273
THE TWO GIRLS IN JEOPARDY
WERE ANNA AND JENASCIA.

149
00:06:13,273 --> 00:06:14,474
Tyra: LET'S DISCUSS ANNA.

150
00:06:14,474 --> 00:06:15,709
I LOVE A PLUS-SIZE GIRL.

151
00:06:15,709 --> 00:06:17,410
SHE HAS A BEAUTIFUL
PLUS-SIZE FIGURE.

152
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:20,313
Eric: HER RUNWAY
DEFINITELY NEEDED SOME WORK.

153
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:22,082
Jenascia: HER REFUSAL
TO DO THE SESSION

154
00:06:22,082 --> 00:06:23,283
DIDN'T WORK FOR ME.

155
00:06:23,283 --> 00:06:26,453
Tyra: JUST BECAUSE
SHE DID NOT DO THE SHOOT,

156
00:06:26,453 --> 00:06:29,155
DOESN'T MEAN THAT
SHE'S AUTOMATICALLY ELIMINATED.

157
00:06:29,155 --> 00:06:30,624
Nigel: IN FACT,
THE GIRL THAT WAS LATE

158
00:06:30,624 --> 00:06:32,425
WAS MORE DAMAGING FOR ME.

159
00:06:32,425 --> 00:06:35,595
Tyra: BUT IN THE END,
IT WAS ANNA WHO WAS SENT HOME.

160
00:06:35,595 --> 00:06:36,630
THANK YOU, ANNA.

161
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:39,566
Anna: THANK YOU, TYRA.

162
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:42,068
YOU KNOW, I CAME HERE
TO PURSUE MODELING

163
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:43,670
AND BE PASSIONATE ABOUT IT,
AND IT'S A TALENT

164
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:45,372
THAT I NEED TO EXPRESS.

165
00:06:45,372 --> 00:06:46,673
I'M NOT GONNA STOP HERE.

166
00:06:46,673 --> 00:06:48,975
THIS IS JUST ANOTHER OBSTACLE
I'M GONNA OVERCOME.

167
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,716
Women: WHOO!

168
00:06:56,716 --> 00:06:59,252
Tyra: AFTER THE FIRST CUT,
IT WAS TIME TO REINTRODUCE

169
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:01,087
THE GIRLS TO J. ALEXANDER.

170
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:02,289
J.: OKAY,
SO I'M GONNA HAVE YOU WALK.

171
00:07:02,289 --> 00:07:03,623
GIRL, DO YOUR THING.

172
00:07:03,623 --> 00:07:05,525
Tyra: ON THE RUNWAY,
THE GIRLS HAD DIFFERENT

173
00:07:05,525 --> 00:07:06,526
STRENGTHS AND WEAKNESSES.

174
00:07:06,526 --> 00:07:07,727
J.: AH, AH, AH!

175
00:07:07,727 --> 00:07:09,696
BRAVO!

176
00:07:09,696 --> 00:07:11,731
GET UP. KEEP ON WALKING, BABY.

177
00:07:11,731 --> 00:07:14,200
Tyra: BETHANY TRIED
TO WORK HER CURVES.

178
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:16,002
Bethany: OBVIOUSLY
I KNOW THAT I DON'T HAVE

179
00:07:16,002 --> 00:07:18,405
A STICK-THIN FIGURE,
BUT QUITE HONESTLY,

180
00:07:18,405 --> 00:07:20,106
NEITHER DOES HALF OF AMERICA.

181
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:23,610
Tyra: SHANDI WAS
INCREDIBLY AWKWARD.

182
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:24,678
J.: HELP.

183
00:07:24,678 --> 00:07:28,248
♪♪♪

184
00:07:28,248 --> 00:07:30,450
Tyra: CAMILLE WAS CONFIDENT.

185
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,518
J.: OH, SEE, I...

186
00:07:31,518 --> 00:07:34,654
SEE, YOU KNOW,
BLACK GIRLS ALWAYS HAVE

187
00:07:34,654 --> 00:07:36,456
TO GIVE THAT EXTRA.

188
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:40,260
Tyra: AND YOANNA LOOKED
LIKE THE WALKING DEAD.

189
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:42,729
J.: YOUR WALK IS REALLY--
IT'S AS USELESS AS A FLASHLIGHT

190
00:07:42,729 --> 00:07:43,730
WITH NO BATTERIES IN THE DARK.

191
00:07:43,730 --> 00:07:45,699
Camille: (laughs)

192
00:07:45,699 --> 00:07:47,534
Tyra: AND AFTER
THE RUNWAY LESSON,

193
00:07:47,534 --> 00:07:50,370
TENSIONS EXPLODED
BETWEEN CAMILLE AND YOANNA.

194
00:07:50,370 --> 00:07:52,105
Camille: FOR REAL,
IF I HAVE SOMETHING

195
00:07:52,105 --> 00:07:53,540
TO SAY TO YOU,
I WILL SAY IT TO YOUR FACE.

196
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:56,109
Yoanna: THE LAST COUPLE TIMES
THAT YOU'VE HAD THINGS TO SAY

197
00:07:56,109 --> 00:07:57,377
ABOUT ME, YOU'VE NEVER SAID IT
TO MY FACE, AND WHEN

198
00:07:57,377 --> 00:07:59,612
I'VE CONFRONTED YOU ABOUT IT--

199
00:07:59,612 --> 00:08:02,048
Camille: I HAVEN'T SAID
ANYTHING TO YOU--

200
00:08:02,048 --> 00:08:03,516
Yoanna: OKAY, OKAY, ENJOY.

201
00:08:03,516 --> 00:08:04,617
Camille: AND TRUST ME, IF I HAVE
SOMETHING TO SAY TO YOU--

202
00:08:04,617 --> 00:08:06,019
Yoanna: I DON'T TRUST YOU!

203
00:08:06,019 --> 00:08:07,454
Camille: I WILL SAY IT
TO YOUR FACE.

204
00:08:07,454 --> 00:08:09,322
- Yoanna: I DO NOT TRUST YOU.
- Camille: WELL, THAT'S MY WORD.

205
00:08:09,322 --> 00:08:11,291
IF YOU DON'T TRUST ME,
STAY AWAY FROM ME.

206
00:08:11,291 --> 00:08:12,692
Tyra: AND THOSE TENSIONS
CARRIED OVER

207
00:08:12,692 --> 00:08:14,260
TO A HOUSE MEETING.

208
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:15,462
Yoanna: IT IS GETTING
TO THE POINT WHERE IT IS

209
00:08:15,462 --> 00:08:19,432
SO NEGATIVE IN THIS HOUSE,
THE ENERGY IS DRIVING ME CRAZY.

210
00:08:19,432 --> 00:08:21,968
IT'S LIKE WE HAVE TO OPEN
THE WINDOWS AND LET--

211
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:23,370
JUST, WAIT! I'M NOT FINISHED!

212
00:08:23,370 --> 00:08:25,105
Camille: WHERE DOES THAT HATE
AND THE ANGER COME FROM?

213
00:08:25,105 --> 00:08:26,706
I WANT TO KNOW
WHERE THAT ANGER COMES FROM,

214
00:08:26,706 --> 00:08:29,576
BECAUSE I DON'T HAVE THAT ANGER
INSIDE OF ME FOR ANYONE.

215
00:08:29,576 --> 00:08:31,044
I SAID, "IF I HAVE
SOMETHING TO SAY TO YOU,

216
00:08:31,044 --> 00:08:32,679
I'LL SAY IT TO YOUR FACE,"
AND THAT WAS THAT.

217
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:36,683
OTHER THAN THAT, I'M SAYING
STAY... OUT OF MY WAY.

218
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:39,152
Tyra: BETHANY HAD
SOME OF HER OWN CONCERNS,

219
00:08:39,152 --> 00:08:41,121
WHICH SHE CONFIDED TO ME
THAT NIGHT.

220
00:08:41,121 --> 00:08:42,188
Bethany: I WANT SOMETHING
TO WORK ON.

221
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:43,188
I CAN'T DO ANYTHING
ABOUT MY CHEST.

222
00:08:43,188 --> 00:08:44,657
Tyra: YES, YOU CAN.

223
00:08:44,657 --> 00:08:46,626
YOU CAN POSE DIFFERENTLY.

224
00:08:46,626 --> 00:08:48,361
YOU'RE NOT THE ONLY MODEL
THAT HAS A BIG CHEST.

225
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:50,063
Bethany: IF Y'ALL CAN'T STOP
LOOKING AT MY BOOBS

226
00:08:50,063 --> 00:08:52,232
AND START LOOKING AT THE TALENT,
IT'S LIKE, I'M NOT GONNA

227
00:08:52,232 --> 00:08:53,466
SIT HERE AND BE CRITICIZED
OF THE SAME THING.

228
00:08:53,466 --> 00:08:55,068
Tyra: I SUGGEST
YOU LAY OFF THE ATTITUDE.

229
00:08:55,068 --> 00:08:56,603
IT'S NOT NECESSARY,
I'M HERE TO HELP YOU.

230
00:08:56,603 --> 00:08:58,204
I BELIEVE IN EACH
AND EVERY ONE OF YOU,

231
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:00,273
BUT EVERYBODY HAS A FLAW,
AND EVERYBODY NEEDS

232
00:09:00,273 --> 00:09:01,508
TO WORK ON THAT.

233
00:09:01,508 --> 00:09:03,009
AND THAT'S YOUR JOB.

234
00:09:03,009 --> 00:09:04,544
NO MODEL IS PERFECT.

235
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:06,179
YOU LEARN.

236
00:09:08,982 --> 00:09:11,418
THEN IT WAS ON
TO THE SECOND PHOTO SHOOT,

237
00:09:11,418 --> 00:09:13,753
WHERE THE GIRLS HAD
TO STYLE THEMSELVES.

238
00:09:17,357 --> 00:09:19,559
Jay: SO JUST TAKE A STEP
ON THE STAGE.

239
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:23,329
Tyra: BETHANY DID HER BEST
TO CONCEAL HER... ASSETS.

240
00:09:23,329 --> 00:09:24,464
Bethany: OKAY,
TYRA SAID BE CAREFUL

241
00:09:24,464 --> 00:09:26,633
ABOUT POKING MY CHEST OUT.

242
00:09:26,633 --> 00:09:28,068
AND IT'S ABOUT THE SHOES.

243
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:29,269
IT'S REALLY NOT ABOUT ME,
I GUESS.

244
00:09:29,269 --> 00:09:30,537
Jay: YOU GOTTA
GIVE IT TO ME NOW.

245
00:09:30,537 --> 00:09:31,971
Bethany: 55, I GUESS.

246
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:33,706
NO, 94, 94!

247
00:09:33,706 --> 00:09:36,476
Tyra: IN THE END,
THE JUDGES DECIDED THAT BETHANY

248
00:09:36,476 --> 00:09:39,279
WASN'T VERSATILE ENOUGH
FOR FASHION MODELING.

249
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,182
Bethany: I KNOW THAT
I HAVE A LOT MORE TALENT

250
00:09:42,182 --> 00:09:44,217
THAN PROBABLY HALF
OF THESE GIRLS HERE.

251
00:09:44,217 --> 00:09:46,619
IT'S VERY FRUSTRATING TO ME.

252
00:09:46,619 --> 00:09:48,555
THIS IS SOMETHING
I REALLY WANTED.

253
00:09:48,555 --> 00:09:52,025
JUST LEAVE ME... ALONE.

254
00:09:52,025 --> 00:09:53,359
(crying)

255
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:57,564
♪♪♪

256
00:09:57,564 --> 00:10:00,266
Tyra: STILL TO COME--
APRIL FREAKS OUT.

257
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:02,302
April: THEY CAN'T
SNEAK UP ON ME.

258
00:10:02,302 --> 00:10:03,436
Tyra: WE SEE
A WHOLE NEW SIDE OF HEATHER.

259
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:04,537
(laughter)

260
00:10:04,537 --> 00:10:06,573
Tyra: AND IT'S JAY
VERSUS JANICE.

261
00:10:06,573 --> 00:10:07,507
Jay: SHE LOOKS
LIKE A PORNO STAR.

262
00:10:07,507 --> 00:10:08,708
Janice: SO DO YOU.

263
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:14,447
Tyra: I FELT THAT
A LOT OF THE GIRLS

264
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:16,082
NEEDED A DRASTIC MAKEOVER.

265
00:10:16,082 --> 00:10:19,252
SO I SENT THEM TO THE SALON
FOR A MAJOR OVERHAUL.

266
00:10:19,252 --> 00:10:20,553
DO YOU LIKE YOUR CUT?

267
00:10:20,553 --> 00:10:21,988
Yoanna: YES, I LOVE IT.
I REALLY DO.

268
00:10:21,988 --> 00:10:23,256
OH, IT'S PRETTY!

269
00:10:23,256 --> 00:10:25,391
IT'S LIGHT AND PRETTY!

270
00:10:25,391 --> 00:10:26,392
Mercedes: I LIKE MY LOOK.

271
00:10:26,392 --> 00:10:28,194
IT'S VIBRANT, IT'S SEXY,
IT'S EDGY.

272
00:10:28,194 --> 00:10:29,662
- Xiomara: I LOVE IT.
- Shandi: WHOO!

273
00:10:29,662 --> 00:10:30,763
Xiomara: I LOVE IT!

274
00:10:30,763 --> 00:10:32,398
Shandi: EVERYTHING'S
COME TOGETHER,

275
00:10:32,398 --> 00:10:34,601
AND I FEEL SO PRETTY RIGHT NOW.

276
00:10:34,601 --> 00:10:36,369
Tyra: BUT CATIE
WASN'T SO HAPPY.

277
00:10:36,369 --> 00:10:38,972
Catie: I LOOK LIKE A BOY!

278
00:10:38,972 --> 00:10:40,373
Tyra: BUT THAT'S GORGEOUS!

279
00:10:40,373 --> 00:10:42,108
DO YOU KNOW THAT A MODEL
THAT HAS SHORT HAIR

280
00:10:42,108 --> 00:10:44,644
AND CAN PULL OFF SHORT HAIR,
MEANS SHE'S TRULY BEAUTIFUL.

281
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:46,546
AND THAT WHEN YOU'RE HIDING
BEHIND HAIR,

282
00:10:46,546 --> 00:10:49,149
IT MEANS YOU'RE JUST COMMON
AND HIDING BEHIND HAIR.

283
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:50,984
THIS IS GORGEOUS!

284
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,685
WAIT TILL YOU HAVE
YOUR MAKEUP DONE!

285
00:10:52,685 --> 00:10:55,288
RIGHT NOW, YEAH,
IT'S A LITTLE OLIVER TWIST,

286
00:10:55,288 --> 00:10:56,589
BUT WHEN THEY STYLE IT

287
00:10:56,589 --> 00:10:58,391
AND YOU GET YOUR MAKEUP DONE,
IT'S GONNA BE SO PRETTY.

288
00:10:58,391 --> 00:10:59,759
BUT YOU'RE NOT GONNA
LOOK LIKE A BOY, GIRL.

289
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:01,427
YOU'VE GOT BOOTY.
YOU'RE GONNA WORK IT OUT.

290
00:11:01,427 --> 00:11:04,397
Catie: (crying)

291
00:11:04,397 --> 00:11:06,032
Tyra: HEATHER, LIKE CATIE,

292
00:11:06,032 --> 00:11:09,502
WAS ALSO 18 AND HAD A LOT
OF CRYING EPISODES,

293
00:11:09,502 --> 00:11:10,737
BUT LITTLE DID WE KNOW,
SHE HAD A LITTLE FREAK

294
00:11:10,737 --> 00:11:13,640
IN HER, TOO.

295
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,707
Heather: (burps)

296
00:11:14,707 --> 00:11:16,643
Catie: WHY IS YOUR SEAT WET?

297
00:11:16,643 --> 00:11:17,677
Heather: 'CAUSE I PEED.

298
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:19,078
Sara: I DARE YOU...
I'LL GIVE YOU...

299
00:11:19,078 --> 00:11:20,747
I SWEAR TO GOD,
I'LL GIVE YOU $5 IF YOU DO IT.

300
00:11:20,747 --> 00:11:22,749
I WAS JUST LIKE,
"I'D BET YOU $5

301
00:11:22,749 --> 00:11:25,218
THAT YOU WON'T RUN AROUND
THIS HOUSE BUTT NAKED."

302
00:11:25,218 --> 00:11:26,719
♪♪♪

303
00:11:37,096 --> 00:11:39,732
Heather: AAH!

304
00:11:39,732 --> 00:11:43,069
(laughter)

305
00:11:43,069 --> 00:11:46,139
Tyra: THEN A TYRA MAIL CAME.

306
00:11:46,139 --> 00:11:47,340
- Xiomara: "VENUSTRAPHOBIA...
- Camille: "VENUSTRAPHOBIA...

307
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,708
Both: "THE FEAR
OF BEAUTIFUL WOMEN.

308
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:51,544
"OPHIDIOPHOBIA--
THE FEAR OF SNAKES.

309
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:54,681
"ALGOPHOBIA--THE FEAR OF PAIN.

310
00:11:54,681 --> 00:11:57,283
WHAT ARE YOU AFRAID OF?
WE'LL FIND OUT TOMORROW."

311
00:11:57,283 --> 00:11:59,619
Tyra: AND APRIL WENT
INTO A PANIC WHEN SHE THOUGHT

312
00:11:59,619 --> 00:12:01,421
THERE WOULD BE SNAKES
AT THE SHOOT.

313
00:12:01,421 --> 00:12:02,689
April: I'M GOING
HOME TOMORROW.

314
00:12:02,689 --> 00:12:05,091
I CAN'T EVEN SAY
THE NAME OF THIS STUFF.

315
00:12:05,091 --> 00:12:07,026
- I'M GOING HOME.
- Catie: WHAT ARE YOU SCARED OF?

316
00:12:07,026 --> 00:12:08,194
April: WHAT THEY PUT
ON THAT PAPER.

317
00:12:08,194 --> 00:12:09,295
Jenascia: LOOK AT ME,
LOOK AT ME, HEY, FOCUS!

318
00:12:09,295 --> 00:12:11,598
LOOK AT ME. COME ON.

319
00:12:11,598 --> 00:12:12,665
April: (wailing)

320
00:12:12,665 --> 00:12:15,201
Jenascia: I PROMISE
I'M RIGHT HERE.

321
00:12:15,201 --> 00:12:16,970
Sara: IT'S OKAY.

322
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:19,505
April: IT'S IN HERE,
IT'S IN HERE, IT'S IN HERE!

323
00:12:19,505 --> 00:12:20,640
Sara: NO, IT'S NOT.
IT'S NOT, IT'S NOT.

324
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:22,075
IT'S FIRE, IT'S FIRE, OKAY?

325
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:23,977
- April: IT'S FIRE?
- Sara: IT'S FIRE.

326
00:12:23,977 --> 00:12:25,044
LOOK AT THE SMOKE.

327
00:12:25,044 --> 00:12:26,379
April: I NEED TO KNOW
WHERE THEY ARE.

328
00:12:26,379 --> 00:12:28,381
THEY CAN'T SNEAK UP ON ME.
THEY CAN'T SNEAK UP ON ME.

329
00:12:28,381 --> 00:12:29,482
Sara: THEY WON'T
SNEAK UP ON YOU.

330
00:12:29,482 --> 00:12:30,617
THERE'S NOTHING HERE.

331
00:12:30,617 --> 00:12:33,586
Jay: GOOD MORNING, GIRLS.

332
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:37,223
WE ARE GOING TO SUSPEND YOU
FROM THIS LEDGE

333
00:12:37,223 --> 00:12:40,126
AND SHOOT YOU GUYS
HANGING OVER THIS HOLE.

334
00:12:40,126 --> 00:12:42,428
Tyra: APRIL BREATHED
A SIGH OF RELIEF,

335
00:12:42,428 --> 00:12:45,565
BUT CATIE'S FEAR OF HEIGHTS
KICKED INTO HIGH GEAR.

336
00:12:45,565 --> 00:12:47,400
Catie: I'M SCARED
OF HEIGHTS, DAD.

337
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:49,135
I WISH YOU COULD BE HERE.

338
00:12:49,135 --> 00:12:50,970
(crying)

339
00:12:50,970 --> 00:12:52,739
Tyra: THE REST OF THE GIRLS
JUMPED RIGHT IN.

340
00:12:52,739 --> 00:12:55,208
Jay: CAN WE BRING HER UP
A LITTLE HIGHER?

341
00:12:55,208 --> 00:13:00,380
♪♪♪

342
00:13:00,380 --> 00:13:01,748
Tyra: HEATHER SHOWED GUTS,

343
00:13:01,748 --> 00:13:03,716
BUT SHE COULDN'T QUITE
NAIL THE POSE.

344
00:13:03,716 --> 00:13:05,385
Jay: GREAT, GIVE ME
THE INTENSITY EYE,

345
00:13:05,385 --> 00:13:06,386
BUT CLOSE YOUR MOUTH.

346
00:13:06,386 --> 00:13:07,720
YEAH, NOW CLOSE YOUR MOUTH.

347
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,355
IT LOOKS GREAT,
AND JUST KEEP YOUR MOUTH CLOSED

348
00:13:09,355 --> 00:13:10,390
THE WHOLE TIME.

349
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:13,092
CLOSE THE MOUTH.

350
00:13:13,092 --> 00:13:16,262
Tyra: XIOMARA GAVE CATIE
EMOTIONAL SUPPORT.

351
00:13:16,262 --> 00:13:17,430
Xiomara: DO YOU WANT ME
TO GO BEFORE YOU, CATIE?

352
00:13:17,430 --> 00:13:19,432
IT'S ALL GOOD, IT'S ALL GOOD.

353
00:13:19,432 --> 00:13:22,168
IT'S CAKE, BABY.

354
00:13:22,168 --> 00:13:25,004
Tyra: AND FINALLY CATIE
GOT INTO THE HARNESS...

355
00:13:25,004 --> 00:13:28,107
Jay: ALL RIGHT,
JUST LOOK AT ME RIGHT HERE.

356
00:13:28,107 --> 00:13:32,245
THAT'S IT, THAT'S IT.
IT'S OKAY.

357
00:13:32,245 --> 00:13:33,379
DO YOU WANT TO COME UP, CATIE?

358
00:13:33,379 --> 00:13:35,048
- Catie: GIVE ME A SECOND.
- Jay: OKAY.

359
00:13:35,048 --> 00:13:38,151
Tyra: AND MOMENTARILY
MASTERED HER FEAR.

360
00:13:38,151 --> 00:13:40,086
Jay: NO ONE ELSE TALK,
JUST ME.

361
00:13:40,086 --> 00:13:43,556
OKAY, BEAUTIFUL. I LOVE IT.

362
00:13:43,556 --> 00:13:45,458
DO YOU KNOW WHAT, CATIE?
YOU GOT IT.

363
00:13:45,458 --> 00:13:47,327
YOU'RE DONE.
YOU ARE SO DONE.

364
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:49,228
(cheers and applause)

365
00:13:49,228 --> 00:13:53,166
Tyra: AT JUDGING, XIOMARA'S
ACT OF KINDNESS BACKFIRED.

366
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,535
Eric: THERE'S SOMETHING
THAT JUST ISN'T CONNECTING.

367
00:13:55,535 --> 00:13:57,337
IT JUST LOOKS SLOPPY.

368
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:58,471
Xiomara: I DIDN'T REALLY
HAVE MUCH DIRECTION

369
00:13:58,471 --> 00:13:59,572
IN ALL DUE HONESTY
AND FAIRNESS TO YOU,

370
00:13:59,572 --> 00:14:01,107
BECAUSE HE WAS COMFORTING CATIE.

371
00:14:01,107 --> 00:14:02,508
I WAS OUT THERE BY MYSELF.

372
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:04,610
Catie: I HAVE A LITTLE WORD
TO SAY.

373
00:14:04,610 --> 00:14:06,179
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

374
00:14:06,179 --> 00:14:08,147
YOU REALIZE, YES,
JAY WAS SITTING NEXT TO ME

375
00:14:08,147 --> 00:14:09,282
FOR MOST OF THE PART.

376
00:14:09,282 --> 00:14:12,418
THE ENTIRE TIME
HE NEVER SAID A WORD TO ME.

377
00:14:12,418 --> 00:14:15,421
HE WAS DIRECTING XIOMARA.

378
00:14:15,421 --> 00:14:16,556
Xiomara: HE WAS DIRECTING ME,

379
00:14:16,556 --> 00:14:17,757
BUT HE WAS ALSO COMFORTING YOU,
AS WELL.

380
00:14:17,757 --> 00:14:19,225
IT WAS REALLY CONFUSING.
IT WAS REALLY WEIRD.

381
00:14:19,225 --> 00:14:20,727
THE ENERGY WAS...

382
00:14:20,727 --> 00:14:22,028
AND I WAS COMFORTING YOU
WHEN YOU WERE GOING UP, TOO,

383
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:23,730
AND YOU KNOW THAT,
AND YOU KNOW WHAT I SAID TO YOU.

384
00:14:23,730 --> 00:14:25,465
Janice: BOARDING SCHOOL,
BOARDING SCHOOL.

385
00:14:25,465 --> 00:14:27,433
I DON'T CARE
WHAT YOU GUYS DID ON THE SET.

386
00:14:27,433 --> 00:14:30,636
OH, MY GOD.
DRAMA, DRAMA.

387
00:14:30,636 --> 00:14:32,505
Tyra: THE TENSION
CONTINUED BACKSTAGE.

388
00:14:32,505 --> 00:14:34,974
Camille: CAN WE GET
SOME WATER?

389
00:14:34,974 --> 00:14:36,175
April: WE NEED A FAN
OR SOMETHING.

390
00:14:36,175 --> 00:14:37,643
Yoanna: HERE, COME OUT
IN THE FRESH AIR.

391
00:14:37,643 --> 00:14:39,112
April: YOU NEED A FAN
OR SOMETHING?

392
00:14:39,112 --> 00:14:41,614
Yoanna: AFTER THE JUDGING,
CATIE JUST KIND OF GOT

393
00:14:41,614 --> 00:14:42,749
WEAK AND FAINT.

394
00:14:42,749 --> 00:14:44,417
Sara: THERE WAS
THIS BIG PRODUCTION WITH HER

395
00:14:44,417 --> 00:14:46,586
GETTING FANNED AND WATER,
AND I THOUGHT IT WAS HILARIOUS.

396
00:14:46,586 --> 00:14:48,354
Tyra: IT WASN'T ONLY
THE GIRLS WHO GOT INTO IT.

397
00:14:48,354 --> 00:14:52,592
SOMETIMES THE JUDGES HAD,
WELL, A DIFFERENCE OF OPINION.

398
00:14:52,592 --> 00:14:54,327
Jay: I HAD TO FIGHT
WITH HEATHER ON THIS SHOOT

399
00:14:54,327 --> 00:14:56,262
JUST TO GET
HER FACIAL EXPRESSION

400
00:14:56,262 --> 00:14:58,164
TO LOOK SOMEWHAT LIKE A MODEL.

401
00:14:58,164 --> 00:14:59,332
SHE LOOKS LIKE A PORNO STAR.

402
00:14:59,332 --> 00:15:00,700
Janice: NO, SHE DOES NOT!

403
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:03,202
- Jay: YES, SHE DOES.
- Janice: SO DO YOU.

404
00:15:03,202 --> 00:15:05,671
Jay: WE'RE TALKING
SILICONE VALLEY

405
00:15:05,671 --> 00:15:07,573
- AT THE OTHER END OF THE TABLE.
- Janice: WELL, STAND UP!

406
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:09,075
LET'S SEE THE GIRDLE
YOU'RE WEARING.

407
00:15:09,075 --> 00:15:10,643
Jay: JANICE, YOURS IS ALREADY
SURGICALLY CINCHED.

408
00:15:10,643 --> 00:15:12,345
I SNAP ONE THREAD,
AND IT'S DOWN.

409
00:15:12,345 --> 00:15:13,646
Janice: HONEY,
LOOK AT YOUR FACE, PLEASE,

410
00:15:13,646 --> 00:15:15,148
AND YOUR DYED HAIR, PLEASE.

411
00:15:15,148 --> 00:15:17,083
Jay: OKAY.

412
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:19,118
Tyra: THINGS COOLED OFF
WHEN CATIE AND XIOMARA

413
00:15:19,118 --> 00:15:20,353
TALKED IT OUT
JUST BEFORE THE ELIMINATION.

414
00:15:20,353 --> 00:15:21,988
Catie: YOU KNOW WHAT?

415
00:15:21,988 --> 00:15:24,724
I THINK BECAUSE OF ME, THOUGH,
I FEEL LIKE NOBODY GOT 100%.

416
00:15:24,724 --> 00:15:26,993
Xiomara: NO,
IT'S NOT BECAUSE OF YOU, CATIE.

417
00:15:26,993 --> 00:15:28,628
IT'S JUST THAT JAY
DIDN'T GIVE ME ANYTHING.

418
00:15:28,628 --> 00:15:30,329
THAT'S ALL.
IT'S OKAY, IT'S NOT YOU.

419
00:15:30,329 --> 00:15:31,731
I WASN'T SAYING
ANYTHING ABOUT YOU.

420
00:15:31,731 --> 00:15:33,132
Heather: BESIDES, CATIE,
IT WAS JAY'S DECISION

421
00:15:33,132 --> 00:15:34,367
TO COMFORT YOU.

422
00:15:34,367 --> 00:15:35,601
Catie: IF I WOULD HAVE
BEEN THINKING LOGICALLY,

423
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:37,270
I WOULD HAVE TOLD HIM,
"NO, SHE DESERVES MORE."

424
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:38,704
YOU KNOW THAT, RIGHT?

425
00:15:38,704 --> 00:15:40,273
Xiomara: I KNOW, THAT'S OKAY.
I WASN'T TRYING TO, LIKE...

426
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:41,374
Catie: WHY ARE YOU CRYING?

427
00:15:41,374 --> 00:15:43,075
Xiomara: BECAUSE YOU PASSED OUT.

428
00:15:43,075 --> 00:15:45,278
- Camille: COME ON.
- Catie: I DID NOT!

429
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:47,480
Tyra: IN THE END,
HEATHER'S LIMITATIONS

430
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:51,117
OUTWEIGHED XIOMARA'S
AND HEATHER WAS SENT HOME.

431
00:15:51,117 --> 00:15:52,718
Heather: THERE'S A LOT
MORE PEOPLE THAT DESERVE

432
00:15:52,718 --> 00:15:54,687
TO GO HOME RATHER THAN ME.

433
00:15:54,687 --> 00:15:57,156
I KNOW THAT
I'M PRETTIER THAN A LOT OF

434
00:15:57,156 --> 00:16:01,427
THOSE GIRLS STANDING UP THERE,
AND THAT'S THE ONLY REASON

435
00:16:01,427 --> 00:16:02,728
WHY IT WOULD EVER HURT.

436
00:16:02,728 --> 00:16:06,332
(sniffling)

437
00:16:08,401 --> 00:16:11,237
Tyra: SPENDING ALL THEIR TIME
TOGETHER INEVITABLY LED

438
00:16:11,237 --> 00:16:12,438
TO PETTY ARGUMENTS.

439
00:16:12,438 --> 00:16:14,340
Catie: OUR SINK WAS CLOGGED.

440
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:15,641
THEN OUR BATHROOM WAS CLOGGED.

441
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:17,443
Yoanna: WE WERE
SCRUBBING AND CLEANING,

442
00:16:17,443 --> 00:16:18,711
AND CAMILLE WAS ON THE PHONE.

443
00:16:18,711 --> 00:16:21,113
Catie: LET ME TELL YOU
ABOUT MISS DIVA.

444
00:16:21,113 --> 00:16:22,348
Camille: IF EVERYBODY
WANTS TO CLEAN IN A GROUP,

445
00:16:22,348 --> 00:16:24,417
THEN COME LET ME KNOW
THAT YOU'RE CLEANING IN GROUPS,

446
00:16:24,417 --> 00:16:26,085
SO THEN I CAN PARTICIPATE.

447
00:16:26,085 --> 00:16:27,987
BUT LAST NIGHT, I GUESS
THAT BEFORE WHEN EVERYBODY

448
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:31,123
WAS IN THEIR BEDS SLEEPING,
I TOOK TWO HOURS OUT

449
00:16:31,123 --> 00:16:34,026
OF MY SLEEP SCHEDULE TO CLEAN,
BECAUSE THE PLACE WAS DIRTY.

450
00:16:34,026 --> 00:16:36,629
Catie: THOSE EXPLANATIONS
ARE ALWAYS INCREDIBLY,

451
00:16:36,629 --> 00:16:38,264
INCREDIBLY LONG.

452
00:16:38,264 --> 00:16:40,233
Camille: I DO CLEAN,
SO I DON'T WANT TO MAKE IT SEEM

453
00:16:40,233 --> 00:16:42,502
LIKE, OH, I'M NOT PARTICIPATING
IN THE HOUSE BEING CLEAN,

454
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:43,736
'CAUSE I DO.

455
00:16:43,736 --> 00:16:46,005
I JUST DO IT ALL BY MYSELF.

456
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,173
Catie: WELL, I'M SURE
YOU CAN LOOK AROUND

457
00:16:47,173 --> 00:16:49,542
AND FIND SOMETHING
THAT YOU CAN CLEAN.

458
00:16:49,542 --> 00:16:51,344
Camille: I MEAN,
THAT'S WHY I DID

459
00:16:51,344 --> 00:16:53,212
WHAT I DID YESTERDAY.

460
00:16:53,212 --> 00:16:54,547
Catie: UGH!

461
00:16:54,547 --> 00:16:55,348
Tyra: THE GIRLS
GOT AN INVALUABLE LESSON

462
00:16:55,348 --> 00:16:56,983
IN PERSONAL STYLE.

463
00:16:56,983 --> 00:17:00,486
AND I HAVE MY BUDDY HERE,
MR. SIMON DOONAN.

464
00:17:00,486 --> 00:17:03,689
SIMON IS THE CREATIVE DIRECTOR
OF BARNEY'S NEW YORK.

465
00:17:03,689 --> 00:17:06,192
Simon: IN ORDER FOR YOU GUYS
TO DEVELOP YOUR OWN STYLE,

466
00:17:06,192 --> 00:17:07,560
WE HAVE TO PLAY
THE BRANDING GAME.

467
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:09,194
SEE ALL THESE WORDS?

468
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:12,598
YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE
ONE MINUTE TO GRAB THE WORDS

469
00:17:12,598 --> 00:17:13,665
THAT PERTAIN TO YOU.

470
00:17:13,665 --> 00:17:15,134
GO!

471
00:17:15,134 --> 00:17:20,339
♪♪♪

472
00:17:20,339 --> 00:17:24,277
- Sara: I PICKED EXOTIC.
- Simon: AS IN DANCER.

473
00:17:24,277 --> 00:17:25,344
Shandi: I DON'T KNOW. I THINK
I KINDA HAVE A NERDY,

474
00:17:25,344 --> 00:17:27,079
LITTLE GEEKY STYLE.

475
00:17:27,079 --> 00:17:30,583
Mercedes: COQUETTISH,
'CAUSE I JUST LEARNED THE WORD.

476
00:17:30,583 --> 00:17:32,318
Simon: WELL,
WHAT ARE THE THREE WORDS

477
00:17:32,318 --> 00:17:35,087
THAT YOU WOULD DESCRIBE
AS WHAT YOU'RE WEARING TODAY?

478
00:17:35,087 --> 00:17:36,122
Catie: I DON'T--
I REALLY DON'T KNOW.

479
00:17:36,122 --> 00:17:37,557
I'M... I'VE ALWAYS--

480
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:41,260
Simon: WERE YOU HAVING A BREAK
WITH REALITY WHEN YOU GOT READY?

481
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:43,462
I THINK THERE'S A LITTLE
TOO MUCH HOOKER STYLE GOING ON

482
00:17:43,462 --> 00:17:45,097
WITH THE LEG WARMERS
WITH THE HIGH HEELS.

483
00:17:45,097 --> 00:17:47,133
GO DOWN WHERE THE HOOKERS
HANG OUT BY THE DOCKS

484
00:17:47,133 --> 00:17:49,435
AND SEE WHAT THEY'RE WEARING,
AND THEN AVOID IT.

485
00:17:49,435 --> 00:17:52,204
SOMETHING THAT
YOU GUYS HAVE TO BECOME

486
00:17:52,204 --> 00:17:54,040
COMFORTABLE WITH--
BEING SELF-CRITICAL,

487
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:55,641
BEING CRITICAL OF EACH OTHER.

488
00:17:55,641 --> 00:17:57,343
AND WHAT I GET
FROM SOME OF YOU GUYS

489
00:17:57,343 --> 00:17:59,512
IS THAT YOU CAN'T YET DO THAT.

490
00:17:59,512 --> 00:18:02,481
IN PARTICULAR YOU,
YOU SEEM TO BE GETTING

491
00:18:02,481 --> 00:18:03,549
KIND OF IRATE, BECAUSE--

492
00:18:03,549 --> 00:18:05,451
Catie: YOU CALLED ME A HO!

493
00:18:05,451 --> 00:18:07,420
Simon: I WOULD NEVER
SAY ANYBODY WAS A HO.

494
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:12,358
I WOULD SAY, "THAT'S HO STYLE."

495
00:18:12,358 --> 00:18:15,161
YOU HAVE TO GET USED TO THE FACT
THAT IT'S NOT REALLY ABOUT YOU.

496
00:18:15,161 --> 00:18:17,496
Catie: IF IT WAS YOU
AND ME TALKING, THAT'S COOL.

497
00:18:17,496 --> 00:18:19,332
Simon: EXCEPT YOU KNEW
WHEN YOU ENTERED

498
00:18:19,332 --> 00:18:21,434
INTO THIS COMPETITION
THAT YOU'RE NOT GONNA SIT THERE

499
00:18:21,434 --> 00:18:23,135
FOR THREE WEEKS
WITH AN UMBRELLA DRINK

500
00:18:23,135 --> 00:18:25,204
WITH EVERYBODY TELLING YOU
HOW FABULOUS YOU ARE.

501
00:18:25,204 --> 00:18:26,572
Catie: NO, I DIDN'T EXPECT
THAT AT ALL, BUT I JUST--

502
00:18:26,572 --> 00:18:28,274
Simon: BUT IT SOUNDS
LIKE YOU DID.

503
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:31,077
Tyra: WHILE CATIE'S PROBLEMS
WERE OUT IN THE OPEN,

504
00:18:31,077 --> 00:18:34,680
MERCEDES KEPT HERS INSIDE.

505
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:37,116
Mercedes: RECENTLY
AT THE HOUSE MY HAIR

506
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:40,386
HAS BEEN FALLING OUT
BECAUSE OF THE HIGH MEDICATION.

507
00:18:40,386 --> 00:18:43,122
I WAS DIAGNOSED WITH LUPUS,
WHICH IS A CHRONIC ILLNESS

508
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:45,157
WHERE IT ATTACKS
YOUR IMMUNE SYSTEM,

509
00:18:45,157 --> 00:18:48,060
ABOUT A YEAR AGO,
AND IT PRETTY MUCH

510
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:50,096
CHANGED MY LIFE.

511
00:18:50,096 --> 00:18:51,731
IT'S BEST TO KEEP IT A SECRET,
'CAUSE I DON'T WANT THEM

512
00:18:51,731 --> 00:18:53,299
TO TALK ABOUT,
"OH, HOW ARE YOU FEELING?

513
00:18:53,299 --> 00:18:54,767
OH, THIS MUST BE HARD."

514
00:18:54,767 --> 00:18:56,669
YOU KNOW, DON'T GIVE ME THAT.
I DON'T NEED IT.

515
00:18:56,669 --> 00:18:58,738
Tyra: WITH THE PHOTO SHOOT
COMING UP THE NEXT DAY,

516
00:18:58,738 --> 00:19:01,207
MERCEDES' ANXIETY WAS HIGH.

517
00:19:01,207 --> 00:19:02,541
- Mercedes' mom: Hello?
- Mercedes: HI, MOM.
HOW ARE YOU?

518
00:19:02,541 --> 00:19:03,976
Mercedes' mom: You okay?

519
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:06,679
Mercedes: MY HAIR IS
CONTINUING TO FALL OUT...

520
00:19:06,679 --> 00:19:08,748
LIKE, A LOT.

521
00:19:08,748 --> 00:19:11,183
IT'S A LOT OF STRESS,
AND WHEN YOU HAVE LUPUS,

522
00:19:11,183 --> 00:19:13,285
YOU CAN'T STRESS OUT,
AND IT'S DIFFICULT TO DO

523
00:19:13,285 --> 00:19:15,554
IN THIS HOUSE,
BECAUSE IT'S VERY STRESSFUL.

524
00:19:15,554 --> 00:19:16,589
PLEASE, TELL ME--

525
00:19:16,589 --> 00:19:18,991
IT'S COMING OUT,
AND I'M SCARED.

526
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:21,427
Mercedes' mom: Okay.
Don't be scared, okay?

527
00:19:21,427 --> 00:19:23,062
Mercedes: I'M JUST
TRYING TO JUST, LIKE, KEEP ON

528
00:19:23,062 --> 00:19:24,296
PUSHING MYSELF, BECAUSE...

529
00:19:24,296 --> 00:19:26,532
YOU KNOW, I'M JUST TRYING
TO STICK IN THERE.

530
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:34,473
Tyra: STILL TO COME--
THE COMPETITION GETS

531
00:19:34,473 --> 00:19:36,008
VERY EMOTIONAL...

532
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:37,410
Yoanna: I WAS SO CHUBBY
AND FAT.

533
00:19:37,410 --> 00:19:40,312
Tyra: AND JANICE ASKS
SOME TOUGH QUESTIONS.

534
00:19:40,312 --> 00:19:43,215
Janice: IF A PHOTOGRAPHER
OFFERED YOU GUARANTEED FAME

535
00:19:43,215 --> 00:19:45,251
IF YOU SLEPT WITH HIM,
WHAT WOULD YOU DO?

536
00:19:45,251 --> 00:19:46,018
April: IS HE ATTRACTIVE?

537
00:19:48,104 --> 00:19:50,756
♪♪♪

538
00:19:50,756 --> 00:19:51,691
Tyra: THEY'VE DONE
SOME VERY CREATIVE

539
00:19:51,691 --> 00:19:53,459
AND AMAZING PHOTO SHOOTS.

540
00:19:53,459 --> 00:19:55,461
ONE OF THE MOST CHALLENGING
WAS WHEN THE GIRLS

541
00:19:55,461 --> 00:19:58,097
HAD TO IMPERSONATE CELEBRITIES.

542
00:19:58,097 --> 00:19:59,498
Mercedes: OKAY,
I'M REALLY SICK.

543
00:19:59,498 --> 00:20:01,367
I JUST FEEL
LIKE I'M GONNA FAINT.

544
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:04,236
I'M JUST REALLY TIRED,
BUT I'M TRYING TO HIDE IT.

545
00:20:04,236 --> 00:20:06,405
Andrew: JUST SORT OF
CUP IT WITH YOUR HAND.

546
00:20:06,405 --> 00:20:07,640
YEP, GOOD.

547
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:09,608
MERCEDES SEEMED NERVOUS.

548
00:20:09,608 --> 00:20:11,410
I DETECTED THAT
SHE WAS EVEN SHAKING

549
00:20:11,410 --> 00:20:12,578
JUST A LITTLE BIT.

550
00:20:12,578 --> 00:20:14,013
Tyra: JUST...
(exhales)

551
00:20:14,013 --> 00:20:15,314
Andrew: GOOD.

552
00:20:15,314 --> 00:20:16,682
Tyra: THERE YOU GO.

553
00:20:16,682 --> 00:20:18,417
Jay: MERCEDES,
IT'S JUST EXACTLY WHAT WE NEED.

554
00:20:18,417 --> 00:20:20,519
- Tyra: YEAH.
- Andrew: NICE.

555
00:20:20,519 --> 00:20:21,353
Mercedes: I PRAY
TO GOD EVERY TIME.

556
00:20:21,353 --> 00:20:25,091
I ASK HIM TO PUT
A LITTLE "OOMPH" IN FOR ME.

557
00:20:26,492 --> 00:20:27,393
Andrew: NICE.

558
00:20:28,761 --> 00:20:41,240
♪♪♪

559
00:20:41,707 --> 00:20:43,309
Jenascia: I THINK THEY
MIGHT HAVE PICKED SALMA FOR ME

560
00:20:43,309 --> 00:20:45,077
BECAUSE SHE'S SHORT
AND I'M SHORT AND...

561
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:47,346
Tyra: NOW, JENASCIA,
THE LESS TEETH YOU SHOW,

562
00:20:47,346 --> 00:20:48,981
THE MORE YOU LOOK LIKE
SALMA HAYEK.

563
00:20:48,981 --> 00:20:50,282
Jenascia: DO THIS. DO THIS.

564
00:20:50,282 --> 00:20:52,551
OH, OH, OH, OH.

565
00:20:52,551 --> 00:20:54,553
Tyra: JENASCIA'S ATTITUDE
ON SET DIDN'T SCORE POINTS

566
00:20:54,553 --> 00:20:55,988
WITH ANYONE.

567
00:20:55,988 --> 00:20:57,256
Andrew: IT'S A 2-WAY STREET.

568
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:58,457
IT'S NOT FOR ME TO RUN
ALL THE WAY OVER THERE

569
00:20:58,457 --> 00:21:00,226
AND GRAB EVERYTHING FROM YOU.

570
00:21:00,226 --> 00:21:01,494
SHE PROBABLY HASN'T BEEN
IN FRONT OF THE CAMERA

571
00:21:01,494 --> 00:21:03,429
VERY OFTEN.

572
00:21:03,429 --> 00:21:04,764
Tyra: WHEN J. ALEXANDER
SHOWED UP FOR

573
00:21:04,764 --> 00:21:07,133
AN IMPROMPTU RUNWAY TUTORIAL,

574
00:21:07,133 --> 00:21:08,968
JENASCIA SHOWED
MORE SHORTCOMINGS.

575
00:21:08,968 --> 00:21:12,171
J.: MY PROBLEM WITH YOU
IS IT'S HERE.

576
00:21:12,171 --> 00:21:13,639
THERE'S A VOICE SOMEWHERE
INSIDE THAT WE GOTTA BEAT

577
00:21:13,639 --> 00:21:14,740
OUTTA HERE.

578
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:16,976
I NEED YOUR SHOULDERS LIKE THIS.

579
00:21:16,976 --> 00:21:18,511
Jenascia: SO BASICALLY,
JUST STICK OUT MY BOOBS?

580
00:21:18,511 --> 00:21:20,346
SO ALL I HAD TO DO
WAS STICK OUT MY BOOBS.

581
00:21:20,346 --> 00:21:22,348
YOU COULDN'T HAVE TOLD ME THAT
THE FIRST DAY?

582
00:21:22,348 --> 00:21:24,350
Tyra: THEN IT WAS TIME
FOR THE DELIBERATION.

583
00:21:24,350 --> 00:21:26,085
Janice: SHE'S STILL TOO SHORT.

584
00:21:26,085 --> 00:21:27,353
Tyra: I LIKE
THAT JENASCIA IS SHORT,

585
00:21:27,353 --> 00:21:29,221
BUT, YOU KNOW, WHEN YOU HAVE
THINGS THAT ARE LACKING

586
00:21:29,221 --> 00:21:30,456
NEXT TO THE OTHER GIRLS,

587
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:32,191
YOU HAVE TO HAVE SOMETHING
EXTRA SPECIAL.

588
00:21:32,191 --> 00:21:34,693
BUT JENASCIA WAS SENT HOME
AFTER NOT SHOWING THE JUDGES

589
00:21:34,693 --> 00:21:37,062
ENOUGH OF THAT EXTRA EFFORT
SHE NEEDED

590
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:38,430
TO MAKE UP FOR HER HEIGHT.

591
00:21:38,430 --> 00:21:41,033
Jenascia: THIS HOUSE IS
TOTALLY GONNA SUCK WITHOUT ME.

592
00:21:41,033 --> 00:21:43,569
YOU SEE HOW I'M UPSET
BUT I CAN STILL BE FUNNY?

593
00:21:43,569 --> 00:21:44,470
YOU SEE HOW I DO THAT?

594
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:46,071
I'M... GREAT.

595
00:21:46,071 --> 00:21:47,640
(laughs)

596
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:55,214
Tyra: THE NEXT NIGHT,
AN INTUITIVE PSYCHIC VISITED

597
00:21:55,214 --> 00:21:57,283
THE LOFT THE GIVE THE GIRLS
A READING.

598
00:21:57,283 --> 00:21:59,518
Suzannah: MERCEDES,
YOUR BODY'S TIRED.

599
00:21:59,518 --> 00:22:01,253
YOUR MIND ISN'T.

600
00:22:01,253 --> 00:22:04,690
SOMETIMES YOU WANT TO DO MORE
THAN YOU PHYSICALLY CAN,

601
00:22:04,690 --> 00:22:06,258
SO YOU'RE GONNA BE STRUGGLING.

602
00:22:06,258 --> 00:22:08,327
DO YOU UNDERSTAND THAT?

603
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:10,629
Mercedes: SHE'S DEAD ON,
AND SHE'S JUST DOING THIS

604
00:22:10,629 --> 00:22:12,998
WITH NUMBERS, YOUR BIRTHDAY
AND YOUR NAME.

605
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:16,168
Sara: HOW DO YOU SEE MY FATHER
REACTING TO ME BEING A MODEL?

606
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:18,504
MY DAD IS HALF-IRANIAN,
AND HE CONSIDERS MODELING

607
00:22:18,504 --> 00:22:20,172
PROSTITUTION.

608
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:21,740
Suzannah: HE'S GONNA HATE IT,
BUT HE'S GONNA SECRETLY LOVE IT.

609
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:23,342
Sara: REALLY?

610
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:24,977
Suzannah: MAKE PEACE WITH IT.
LET IT GO.

611
00:22:24,977 --> 00:22:27,446
YOU'VE COME THIS FAR.

612
00:22:27,446 --> 00:22:29,014
Tyra: YOANNA WAS LOOKING
FOR A CONNECTION

613
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:30,683
TO HER GRANDMOTHER.

614
00:22:30,683 --> 00:22:33,419
Yoanna: SHE PASSED AWAY,
AND WE LOVED FASHION TOGETHER,

615
00:22:33,419 --> 00:22:36,255
AND SHE'D WAKE ME UP
EVERY MORNING ON SATURDAYS

616
00:22:36,255 --> 00:22:38,991
TO WATCH ELSA KLENSCH,

617
00:22:38,991 --> 00:22:41,660
AND IF SHE KNEW I WAS HERE,
BECAUSE... (crying)

618
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:43,596
I WAS SO CHUBBY AND FAT

619
00:22:43,596 --> 00:22:46,699
AND I ALWAYS GOT MADE FUN OF,
AND I LOST THE WEIGHT AND...

620
00:22:46,699 --> 00:22:49,602
- Suzannah: YOU'RE BEAUTIFUL.
- Yoanna: AND, UM, I'M SORRY.

621
00:22:49,602 --> 00:22:51,537
I JUST MISS HER SO MUCH.

622
00:22:51,537 --> 00:22:54,540
Suzannah: BUT IT'S HERE
THAT SHE'LL ALWAYS BE WITH YOU.

623
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:56,575
YOU CAN'T KILL
A HEART CONNECTION EVER.

624
00:22:56,575 --> 00:22:58,611
IT NEVER DIES.

625
00:22:58,611 --> 00:23:01,347
Tyra: THE GIRLS'
INTERVIEW SKILLS WERE TESTED

626
00:23:01,347 --> 00:23:04,416
BY THE BRUTALLY HONEST
JANICE DICKINSON.

627
00:23:04,416 --> 00:23:08,287
Janice: IF A PHOTOGRAPHER
OFFERED YOU GUARANTEED FAME

628
00:23:08,287 --> 00:23:10,689
IF YOU SLEPT WITH HIM
FOR A COVER OF A MAGAZINE

629
00:23:10,689 --> 00:23:13,259
OR A MAKEUP CAMPAIGN,
WHAT WOULD YOU DO?

630
00:23:13,259 --> 00:23:14,693
April: IS HE ATTRACTIVE?

631
00:23:14,693 --> 00:23:16,228
Yoanna: NO, THANK YOU. NEXT.

632
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:17,429
Camille: WAS HE FINE?
DID I LIKE HIM?

633
00:23:17,429 --> 00:23:19,098
Sara: HELL, NO,
I WOULD NOT DO THAT.

634
00:23:19,098 --> 00:23:21,133
April: I WOULDN'T NOT DO IT.

635
00:23:21,133 --> 00:23:23,035
Janice: YOU SEEM TO BE
A LITTLE INTIMIDATED BY ME.

636
00:23:23,035 --> 00:23:24,270
DO I MAKE YOU NERVOUS?

637
00:23:24,270 --> 00:23:26,672
Camille: I LOVE YOU.
LIKE, PEOPLE MAY CALL YOU,

638
00:23:26,672 --> 00:23:27,673
YOU KNOW,
"THE BITCH" OR WHATEVER--

639
00:23:27,673 --> 00:23:29,375
Janice: THE BITCH?

640
00:23:29,375 --> 00:23:30,743
I DIDN'T SAY "BITCH,"
BUT ARE THEY CALLING ME A BITCH?

641
00:23:30,743 --> 00:23:33,012
Camille: PEOPLE MAY
CALL YOU THAT.

642
00:23:33,012 --> 00:23:34,480
Janice: YOU KNOW,
THAT WAS REALLY OFFENSIVE TO ME.

643
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:36,715
YOU KNOW,
I'M A MEMBER OF THE P.T.A.

644
00:23:36,715 --> 00:23:39,485
Tyra: AFTER BEING CONFRONTED
ABOUT HER LACK OF ENERGY,

645
00:23:39,485 --> 00:23:42,087
MERCEDES HAD TO DECIDE
WHETHER OR NOT TO COME CLEAN

646
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:43,188
ABOUT HER ILLNESS.

647
00:23:43,188 --> 00:23:44,256
Mercedes: I'M LIKE,
"OH, MY GOSH.

648
00:23:44,256 --> 00:23:46,558
"SHOULD I TELL HER I HAVE LUPUS?

649
00:23:46,558 --> 00:23:47,993
AND I HAVEN'T
BEEN FEELING WELL

650
00:23:47,993 --> 00:23:49,395
AND I'VE BEEN TRYING
TO HIDE IT?"

651
00:23:49,395 --> 00:23:51,730
UM, I DON'T WANNA MAKE EXCUSES
THAT I HAVE AN ILLNESS,

652
00:23:51,730 --> 00:23:52,765
BUT I DO.

653
00:23:52,765 --> 00:23:56,402
UM, I HAVE LUPUS.

654
00:23:56,402 --> 00:23:58,604
Janice: AND DOES THAT
PULL AWAY FROM YOUR ENERGY?

655
00:23:58,604 --> 00:23:59,405
Mercedes: IT DOES.

656
00:23:59,405 --> 00:24:01,507
I'M TRYING REALLY HARD
TO FIGHT THROUGH IT.

657
00:24:01,507 --> 00:24:04,076
IT'S JUST SOMETIMES
I CAN'T CONTROL IT.

658
00:24:04,076 --> 00:24:05,311
I MADE A HUGE DECISION.

659
00:24:05,311 --> 00:24:07,479
I JUST SHARED A LITTLE PART
OF ME THAT I HAVE NEVER SHARED

660
00:24:07,479 --> 00:24:08,981
WITH ANYBODY ELSE.

661
00:24:08,981 --> 00:24:11,050
Janice: ALL RIGHT.
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

662
00:24:11,050 --> 00:24:13,752
Tyra: MERCEDES WON
THE CONTEST AND PICKED SARA

663
00:24:13,752 --> 00:24:16,689
TO SHARE HER PRIZE--
VISITS FROM THEIR MOMS.

664
00:24:16,689 --> 00:24:18,524
Sara: OH, MY GOD!

665
00:24:18,524 --> 00:24:20,993
(screaming)

666
00:24:20,993 --> 00:24:22,394
Tyra: SARA STILL QUESTIONED

667
00:24:22,394 --> 00:24:24,263
HER FATHER'S DISAPPROVAL

668
00:24:24,263 --> 00:24:25,597
AND LOOKED TO HER MOM
FOR SUPPORT.

669
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:33,372
Sara's mom: IT'S HARD
TO SAY WITH YOUR DAD.

670
00:24:33,372 --> 00:24:36,675
YOU HAVE NO CONTROL OVER WHAT HE
THINKS, SAYS OR ANYTHING, HONEY.

671
00:24:36,675 --> 00:24:39,144
KNOW THAT IT'S CULTURAL.

672
00:24:41,447 --> 00:24:43,015
Sara's mom: SARA, THEY LOVE YOU.

673
00:24:43,015 --> 00:24:44,416
THEY'RE NOT GONNA HATE YOU.

674
00:24:44,416 --> 00:24:47,319
Shandi: WATCHING,
YOU KNOW, MERCEDES AND SARA--

675
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:49,655
IT'S LIKE THEIR MOMS
KNOW THEM THROUGH AND THROUGH,

676
00:24:49,655 --> 00:24:51,991
AND OF COURSE, IT MAKES ME SAD.

677
00:24:51,991 --> 00:24:55,127
IT MAKES ME THINK ABOUT HOW
I'M NOT THAT WAY WITH MY MOM.

678
00:24:55,127 --> 00:24:57,096
Tyra: THEN I BROUGHT
MY MOM TO THE LOFT

679
00:24:57,096 --> 00:24:59,732
TO TALK ABOUT HOW SHE HELPED ME
GET STARTED IN MODELING.

680
00:24:59,732 --> 00:25:01,567
Carolyn: SHE WOULD BEG ME,
"MOM, WOULD YOU TAKE

681
00:25:01,567 --> 00:25:03,168
"SOME PICTURES OF ME?

682
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:05,337
I NEED SOME PICTURES
TO START A PORTFOLIO."

683
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:07,072
YOU KNOW, I DIDN'T KNOW
WHAT I WAS DOING,

684
00:25:07,072 --> 00:25:10,109
AND SHE
PRETTY MUCH DIDN'T EITHER.

685
00:25:10,109 --> 00:25:11,610
BUT THE PHOTOS
CAME OUT REALLY GREAT.

686
00:25:11,610 --> 00:25:12,978
(laughing)

687
00:25:12,978 --> 00:25:14,480
SHE TOOK THOSE PHOTOGRAPHS

688
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:16,582
AND WENT AROUND
TO DIFFERENT AGENCIES.

689
00:25:16,582 --> 00:25:17,750
Tyra: IN LOS ANGELES.

690
00:25:17,750 --> 00:25:18,984
Carolyn: AND HOW MANY
SAID NO?

691
00:25:18,984 --> 00:25:21,153
Tyra: SIX.

692
00:25:21,153 --> 00:25:22,354
Carolyn: THE FIRST SIX
SAID NO.

693
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:23,389
Tyra: YEAH.

694
00:25:23,389 --> 00:25:24,623
Carolyn: AND THEN ONE SAID YES.

695
00:25:24,623 --> 00:25:26,392
Tyra: ON THAT JOURNEY,
YOUR MOMS HAVE THAT

696
00:25:26,392 --> 00:25:29,395
RESPONSIBILITY TO KEEP YOU SANE
BECAUSE THIS BUSINESS IS INSANE.

697
00:25:29,395 --> 00:25:30,596
Yoanna: YEAH.

698
00:25:30,596 --> 00:25:32,765
Tyra: THE NEXT DAY
WAS A PHOTO SHOOT

699
00:25:32,765 --> 00:25:34,433
IN A TANK OF SALT WATER.

700
00:25:34,433 --> 00:25:37,302
♪♪♪

701
00:25:37,302 --> 00:25:38,537
Tyra: WITH HER NEWFOUND
SELF-CONFIDENCE,

702
00:25:38,537 --> 00:25:40,973
SARA NAILED THE SHOOT.

703
00:25:40,973 --> 00:25:43,008
Jay: THE EYES
ARE TEN TIMES BETTER.

704
00:25:43,008 --> 00:25:46,111
Nolé: THAT WAS--
THAT WAS GORGEOUS.

705
00:25:46,111 --> 00:25:47,713
SHE LOOKS BLOATED,
LIKE A FISH.

706
00:25:47,713 --> 00:25:49,748
IT'S GETTING DANGEROUS IN THERE.

707
00:25:49,748 --> 00:25:51,250
THERE'S SOME SHARKS
IN THAT WATER.

708
00:25:51,250 --> 00:25:53,752
♪♪♪

709
00:25:53,752 --> 00:25:55,154
Jay: CAMILLE GOT IN THAT TANK,

710
00:25:55,154 --> 00:25:56,722
AND I WAS
JUST EXPECTING AMAZING.

711
00:25:56,722 --> 00:26:01,160
SHE GAVE ME KIND OF THIS,
LIKE, DRAG QUEEN VOGUE.

712
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:02,394
George: BEAUTIFUL. WOW.

713
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:03,762
GORGEOUS.

714
00:26:03,762 --> 00:26:06,031
Nolé: SHE GAVE YOU
WATER COUTURE, HONEY.

715
00:26:06,031 --> 00:26:07,666
Xiomara: IT'LL BE INTERESTING
TO SEE ME HOLDING MY BREATH

716
00:26:07,666 --> 00:26:09,268
WITHOUT USING MY HANDS.

717
00:26:09,268 --> 00:26:12,671
I'VE TRIED IT, AND WATER
GOES ALL UP IN MY NOSE.

718
00:26:12,671 --> 00:26:15,240
Tyra: XIOMARA HAD
A GORGEOUS, EXOTIC FACE,

719
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:17,076
BUT IN THE MODELING INDUSTRY,
IT'S NOT ABOUT

720
00:26:17,076 --> 00:26:18,477
HOW PRETTY YOU ARE.

721
00:26:18,477 --> 00:26:20,412
IT'S HOW YOU HANDLE
YOUR PHOTO SHOOTS.

722
00:26:20,412 --> 00:26:22,181
Jay: YOUR EYES ARE CLOSED
IN EVERY SHOT.

723
00:26:22,181 --> 00:26:25,317
Nolé: XIOMARA--
ABSOLUTELY GORGEOUS GIRL.

724
00:26:25,317 --> 00:26:28,353
SHE LOOKED LIKE A WALRUS
WEARING CHIFFON.

725
00:26:28,353 --> 00:26:31,090
IT WAS A DISASTER
FROM START TO FINISH.

726
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:32,458
Tyra: AND AT
THE NEXT ELIMINATION,

727
00:26:32,458 --> 00:26:35,194
IT CAME DOWN TO CAMILLE
AND XIOMARA.

728
00:26:35,194 --> 00:26:37,996
Nolé: XIOMARA--SHE LOOKED
LIKE SHE WAS FLOUNDERING,

729
00:26:37,996 --> 00:26:41,033
LIKE A LARGE ANIMAL
IN THE WATER.

730
00:26:41,033 --> 00:26:42,501
IT WAS VERY UNATTRACTIVE.

731
00:26:42,501 --> 00:26:44,970
I THINK XIOMARA IS
ONE OF THE FEW GIRLS

732
00:26:44,970 --> 00:26:48,273
WHO COULD BE DOING
THE COUTURE RUNWAYS IN PARIS.

733
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:50,275
- Nigel: ERIC.
- Nolé: WHAT IS WRONG WITH YOU?

734
00:26:50,275 --> 00:26:52,478
Eric: I THINK
THAT THERE'S POTENTIAL IN THAT.

735
00:26:52,478 --> 00:26:56,248
Tyra: AND IN THE END,
XIOMARA WAS SENT HOME.

736
00:26:56,248 --> 00:26:57,649
Xiomara: OF COURSE
I WANNA STAY HERE.

737
00:26:57,649 --> 00:27:00,385
I DON'T WANNA GO.
I WANNA STAY.

738
00:27:00,385 --> 00:27:02,254
BUT, UM, YOU KNOW,
IF I'M NOT WHAT SOMEONE WANTS,

739
00:27:02,254 --> 00:27:03,622
I'M COOL WITH THAT.

740
00:27:03,622 --> 00:27:05,657
LIKE, I'M NOT GONNA SIT HERE
AND BEAT MYSELF UP BECAUSE

741
00:27:05,657 --> 00:27:07,459
I'M NOT WHAT SOMEONE WANTS.

742
00:27:09,328 --> 00:27:11,330
Tyra: AFTER SURVIVING
NEAR ELIMINATION,

743
00:27:11,330 --> 00:27:13,398
CAMILLE WAS MORE DETERMINED
THAN EVER TO SHOW THE JUDGES

744
00:27:13,398 --> 00:27:14,433
HER STAR POWER.

745
00:27:14,433 --> 00:27:16,201
Camille: SALUD.

746
00:27:16,201 --> 00:27:17,970
Tyra: BUT ON THE MORNING
OF THEIR NEXT PHOTO SHOOT,

747
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:19,505
CAMILLE AWOKE
WITH A BIG PROBLEM.

748
00:27:19,505 --> 00:27:24,109
SHE'D HAD AN ALLERGIC REACTION,
AND HER LIPS WERE SWOLLEN.

749
00:27:24,109 --> 00:27:25,177
Camille: BUT IT'S JUST
GETTING WORSE.

750
00:27:25,177 --> 00:27:27,980
LIKE, IT'S JUST GETTING TIGHTER.

751
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:29,314
Tyra: AS THE GIRLS POSED,

752
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:31,416
CAMILLE HOPED HER LIPS
WOULD HEAL.

753
00:27:31,416 --> 00:27:33,118
- Mercedes: LET ME SEE.
- Camille: I JUST CAN FEEL IT.

754
00:27:33,118 --> 00:27:34,620
Mercedes: I JUST CAN'T
REMEMBER HOW BIG YOUR LIPS

755
00:27:34,620 --> 00:27:36,622
WERE TO BEGIN WITH.

756
00:27:38,590 --> 00:27:40,559
Tyra: EVEN THOUGH CAMILLE
WAS THE ONE WITH THE CRISIS,

757
00:27:40,559 --> 00:27:42,528
WHEN IT CAME TO ACTING CLASS,

758
00:27:42,528 --> 00:27:45,264
SHE WAS THE ONLY ONE
TO HOLD BACK HER EMOTIONS.

759
00:27:45,264 --> 00:27:46,999
Sara: I'M DOING THIS
BECAUSE IF YOU DISOWN ME--

760
00:27:46,999 --> 00:27:48,333
I'M GONNA BE A MODEL.

761
00:27:48,333 --> 00:27:49,568
YOU CAN HATE ME.

762
00:27:49,568 --> 00:27:51,136
Shandi: I DON'T KNOW
ANYONE IN MY FAMILY

763
00:27:51,136 --> 00:27:52,171
BECAUSE OF YOU.

764
00:27:52,171 --> 00:27:53,405
April: YOU'RE--YOU'RE...

765
00:27:53,405 --> 00:27:56,441
Women: (sobbing)

766
00:27:59,444 --> 00:28:03,582
Camille: OH... MY... GOD.

767
00:28:03,582 --> 00:28:06,518
Tyra: IN A LATER EXERCISE,
CAMILLE NOT ONLY REFUSED

768
00:28:06,518 --> 00:28:09,521
TO SHOW EMOTION,
SHE ALSO REWROTE THE SCRIPT.

769
00:28:09,521 --> 00:28:13,091
Camille: I DIDN'T BELIEVE IT,
WHAT THEY TOLD ME.

770
00:28:13,091 --> 00:28:14,059
IT'S TRUE. YOU ARE ALIVE.

771
00:28:14,059 --> 00:28:16,028
Mark: HOW LONG HAS IT BEEN?

772
00:28:16,028 --> 00:28:20,399
Camille: NOT ONE,
NOT TWO, BUT THREE LONG MONTHS.

773
00:28:20,399 --> 00:28:24,236
I CRIED, COLIN,
NOT FOR ONE, NOT FOR TWO,

774
00:28:24,236 --> 00:28:28,974
BUT I CRIED FOR SIX MONTHS.

775
00:28:28,974 --> 00:28:33,045
YOU KNOW ME, LAURA,
STRONG, PROUD,

776
00:28:33,045 --> 00:28:35,380
THE ONE THAT YOU
LOVED AND RESPECTED.

777
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:38,650
I FOCUSED MY ENERGY
INTO SCULPTING.

778
00:28:38,650 --> 00:28:41,386
I EVEN GAVE
SOME AWAY TO CHARITY.

779
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:43,188
WHY DID YOU HAVE TO LEAVE ME,
BABY?

780
00:28:51,530 --> 00:28:53,599
Tasha: I DIDN'T BELIEVE
ANYTHING YOU DID UP THERE--

781
00:28:53,599 --> 00:28:54,633
NOTHING.

782
00:28:54,633 --> 00:28:56,268
I THOUGHT IT WAS HORRIBLE.

783
00:28:56,268 --> 00:28:59,071
(sighs) POOR CAMILLE.

784
00:28:59,071 --> 00:29:01,440
SHE'S CLUELESS.

785
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:03,141
Tyra: NOW CAMILLE WASN'T
THE ONLY GIRL HAVING PROBLEMS

786
00:29:03,141 --> 00:29:04,343
WITH ACTING.

787
00:29:04,343 --> 00:29:06,478
Catie: WHEN THEY TOLD ME
YOUR PLANE WENT DOWN

788
00:29:06,478 --> 00:29:09,181
IN THE JUNGLE...

789
00:29:09,181 --> 00:29:11,516
AND THERE WERE NO SURVIVORS,
I DIDN'T SHED A TEAR.

790
00:29:11,516 --> 00:29:14,253
- Mark: (suppresses chuckle)
- Catie: I'M HALF-ASSING IT.

791
00:29:14,253 --> 00:29:16,722
HOW THE CRAP
CAN I TAKE THIS SERIOUSLY?

792
00:29:21,526 --> 00:29:23,629
Tasha: YOU COULD'VE
KISSED HIM BETTER THAN THAT.

793
00:29:23,629 --> 00:29:25,330
Catie: I CAN'T,
I HAVE A BOYFRIEND.

794
00:29:25,330 --> 00:29:26,365
Tasha: SO WHAT?

795
00:29:26,365 --> 00:29:27,633
THIS IS ABOUT WINNING.

796
00:29:27,633 --> 00:29:29,268
YOU HAVE TO STAY COMMITTED
IN THE SCENE.

797
00:29:29,268 --> 00:29:30,736
I DON'T CARE
ABOUT YOUR BOYFRIEND.

798
00:29:30,736 --> 00:29:32,638
♪ THE FUTURE IS NOW ♪

799
00:29:32,638 --> 00:29:34,139
Tyra: THEN IT WAS TIME

800
00:29:34,139 --> 00:29:35,607
FOR THE GIRLS TO PUT
THEIR NEW ACTING SKILLS

801
00:29:35,607 --> 00:29:38,243
ON THE LINE WHEN THEY SHOT
A HIGH ACTION COMMERCIAL.

802
00:29:40,412 --> 00:29:42,514
Mercedes: AND THERE'S ONLY--
WHAT? (giggles)

803
00:29:42,514 --> 00:29:44,416
Yoanna: THERE WILL ONLY BE
ONE CHOICE.

804
00:29:44,416 --> 00:29:46,485
Camille: (British accent)
FOR AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

805
00:29:46,485 --> 00:29:47,552
Catie: JUST ONE.

806
00:29:47,552 --> 00:29:48,654
Sara: UNO, BABY.

807
00:29:48,654 --> 00:29:50,222
Shandi: SO YOU GOTTA BE TOUGH.

808
00:29:50,222 --> 00:29:51,623
Mercedes: HEY,
A GIRL'S GOTTA DO

809
00:29:51,623 --> 00:29:53,258
WHAT A GIRL'S GOTTA DO.

810
00:29:53,258 --> 00:29:55,627
Jay: TOUGH SUPERHERO,
NOT TOUGH BRONX.

811
00:29:55,627 --> 00:29:57,296
James: YEAH.

812
00:29:57,296 --> 00:29:58,530
Mercedes: I'M FROM JERSEY.

813
00:29:58,530 --> 00:29:59,765
- Sara: (roars)
- Catie: (roars)

814
00:29:59,765 --> 00:30:02,034
- Yoanna: (roars)
- Mercedes: (roars)

815
00:30:02,034 --> 00:30:03,135
James: OKAY. OH, NO.
TOO CUTE.

816
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:04,636
Mercedes: I'M TOO CUTE.

817
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:07,739
Tyra: AT THE ELIMINATION,
CATIE'S MATURITY AND COMMITMENT

818
00:30:07,739 --> 00:30:09,508
WERE QUESTIONED.

819
00:30:09,508 --> 00:30:11,009
Nigel: IT'S AMAZING
HOW YOUNG--YOU REALLY SEE

820
00:30:11,009 --> 00:30:12,678
- THAT YOU'RE 18 YEARS OLD.
- Janice: YOU LOOK 13.

821
00:30:12,678 --> 00:30:17,716
REALLY, REALLY YOUNG,
LIKE CHILD PROSTITUTE.

822
00:30:17,716 --> 00:30:18,617
Eric: SHE'S KIND OF
THE GIRL NEXT DOOR.

823
00:30:18,617 --> 00:30:20,118
Janice: EW.

824
00:30:20,118 --> 00:30:21,453
Eric: BUT I THINK
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL

825
00:30:21,453 --> 00:30:24,489
HAS TO BE, LIKE, THE GIRL, LIKE,
WAY OVER THERE.

826
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:26,191
Tyra: DOWN THE STREET,
AROUND THE CORNER.

827
00:30:26,191 --> 00:30:27,225
Eric: YEAH. EXACTLY.

828
00:30:27,225 --> 00:30:29,628
Tyra: CATIE WAS SENT HOME.

829
00:30:31,063 --> 00:30:33,365
Catie: THANKS, GUYS.

830
00:30:33,365 --> 00:30:35,200
(sobbing)

831
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:37,602
I DON'T FEEL REJECTED.

832
00:30:37,602 --> 00:30:40,305
GO BACK TO L.A.,
WORK MY ASS OFF

833
00:30:40,305 --> 00:30:45,043
AND GET TO THE TOP ON MY OWN.

834
00:30:45,043 --> 00:30:47,279
♪♪♪

835
00:30:49,648 --> 00:30:51,083
♪♪♪

836
00:30:51,083 --> 00:30:52,217
Tyra: STILL TO COME--

837
00:30:52,217 --> 00:30:54,086
THE GIRLS LEARN
SOME NEW MOVES...

838
00:30:54,086 --> 00:30:55,520
Kevin: THAT'S A DIVA, HONEY.

839
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:57,289
Tony: YOU ARE ILLEGAL.

840
00:30:57,289 --> 00:30:59,358
Tyra: AND THE RESULTS
AREN'T ALWAYS PRETTY.

841
00:30:59,358 --> 00:31:00,759
Janice: WHAT THE HELL
WAS THAT?

842
00:31:04,229 --> 00:31:06,064
♪♪♪

843
00:31:10,001 --> 00:31:12,037
Tyra: A TOP MODEL
HAS TO MOVE GRACEFULLY

844
00:31:12,037 --> 00:31:13,472
ON THE RUNWAY,

845
00:31:13,472 --> 00:31:15,440
IN FRONT OF THE CAMERA,
AT PUBLIC APPEARANCES,

846
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:17,142
EVERYWHERE.

847
00:31:17,142 --> 00:31:19,411
IT IS SO IMPORTANT THAT A MODEL
BE ABLE TO EXPRESS HERSELF

848
00:31:19,411 --> 00:31:20,445
THROUGH HER BODY.

849
00:31:22,214 --> 00:31:25,250
SO I PUT THE GIRLS IN THE HANDS
OF CHOREOGRAPHER TONY MICHAELS,

850
00:31:25,250 --> 00:31:27,152
WHO TRIED TO
TEACH THEM SOME MOVES.

851
00:31:27,152 --> 00:31:30,422
♪ WHOA ♪
♪ WHOA... ♪

852
00:31:34,159 --> 00:31:35,494
Camille: CAN I USE A CHAIR?

853
00:31:35,494 --> 00:31:36,695
Tony: NO.
YOU CAN'T USE NO CHAIR.

854
00:31:36,695 --> 00:31:39,398
Yoanna: IMAGINE, IMAGINE--
CAMILLE, CAMILLE,

855
00:31:39,398 --> 00:31:40,699
ALWAYS HAVE TO UP AND UP.

856
00:31:40,699 --> 00:31:42,367
♪ WHOA... ♪♪

857
00:31:42,367 --> 00:31:43,502
Tony: GIRL,
GO ON OVER THERE.

858
00:31:43,502 --> 00:31:47,139
GO ON OVER THERE,
'CAUSE YOU ARE ILLEGAL!

859
00:31:47,139 --> 00:31:49,174
Tyra: THAT NIGHT,
THE GIRLS WERE GIVEN

860
00:31:49,174 --> 00:31:51,410
A LITTLE LESSON
IN RUNWAY STYLE

861
00:31:51,410 --> 00:31:55,247
BY SOME OF NEW YORK CITY'S
MOST DIVA-LICIOUS DRAG QUEENS.

862
00:31:55,247 --> 00:31:58,083
LET'S PARTY!

863
00:31:58,083 --> 00:31:59,184
♪♪♪

864
00:31:59,184 --> 00:32:01,086
Tyra: IT IS IMPOSSIBLE

865
00:32:01,086 --> 00:32:03,054
TO IGNORE A DRAG QUEEN
ON THE RUNWAY,

866
00:32:03,054 --> 00:32:05,390
AND I WANTED TO INSPIRE
THE GIRLS IN THE WAY

867
00:32:05,390 --> 00:32:08,460
THAT THEY MOVE, DANCE,
AND JUST PLAIN WORK IT.

868
00:32:08,460 --> 00:32:09,594
Kevin: LOOK AT THEM.

869
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:11,163
LOOK AT
THEIR FACIAL EXPRESSIONS.

870
00:32:11,163 --> 00:32:12,764
LOOK AT THEIR EYES.

871
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:14,199
LOOK AT THE WAY
THEY'RE USING THEIR SHOULDERS.

872
00:32:14,199 --> 00:32:16,334
DO YOU SEE HOW SHE WALKED ON?

873
00:32:16,334 --> 00:32:17,369
DID YOU SEE THAT?

874
00:32:17,369 --> 00:32:19,070
THAT'S A DIVA, HONEY.

875
00:32:19,070 --> 00:32:20,372
DID YOU SEE THE WAY
SHE WALKED ON?

876
00:32:20,372 --> 00:32:21,573
NOW IT'S YOUR TURN.

877
00:32:21,573 --> 00:32:22,674
Tyra: GET UP!

878
00:32:22,674 --> 00:32:24,242
♪♪♪

879
00:32:24,242 --> 00:32:25,343
Tyra: ♪ GO, APRIL ♪

880
00:32:25,343 --> 00:32:27,012
♪ GO, APRIL ♪

881
00:32:27,012 --> 00:32:30,515
♪ GO, SHANDI, GO, SHANDI ♪

882
00:32:30,515 --> 00:32:33,351
♪ GO, MERCEDES, WORK IT OUT ♪♪

883
00:32:34,486 --> 00:32:37,689
Tyra: WHOO! WORK IT OUT!

884
00:32:37,689 --> 00:32:42,127
